  "term": "S and M",
  "definition": "In this source, \"S and M\" refers to two retinal cone classes identified by their opsins: S-cones and M/L-cones. These are light-sensitive cone cells whose degeneration patterns were examined in a mouse model of retinitis pigmentosa.",
